# Jail-boundary V2 rig: acceptance tests for swxtchio/swx-abbe#1952 and #1953

The rig answers two questions about the Orch OpenCode jail. It runs the real jail daemon behind the
real egress proxy, and it sends the V2 calls exactly as Abbe's `opencode_client.py` sends them.

- **#1952: does a V2 chat turn reach the `swxtch-egress` provider?** Modes `v1-control`, `v2` and
  `v2-named` pass only if the fake provider receives the turn's model request. All three pass from
  `v1.18.32-swxtch.cd3f0ce2`; on `v1.18.32-swxtch.774d90c7` the two V2 modes reached no provider.
- **#1953: does a V2 compaction complete through the jail?** Mode `compact` passes only if the fake
  provider receives the summary request and the session records the finished compaction. It is the
  acceptance proof for #1953's fix, swxtchio/swx-opencode#354. On `cd3f0ce2` it fails: the compact call
  answers 503. That run is the red baseline in §6.

## What runs

The rig is `_brain_rig` in swx-abbe's
`components/orch/services/opencode-variant/tests/test_opencode_jail_integration.py`. The probe uses
it as it is: `compact` passes its own provider through the rig's existing `provider_code=` argument,
so the rig needs no repository change. The rig puts three containers on a new internal Docker network:

1. **The jail daemon, from the image under test.** The image's own entrypoint
   (`/jail/opencode_server.py`) reads `OPENCODE_CONFIG=/jail/opencode.json` and renders it with the
   proxy URL and the session capability, which the rig passes as `OPENCODE_PROXY_BASE_URL` and
   `OPENCODE_PROXY_CAPABILITY`, into `OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT`. It then execs
   `opencode serve --pure`.
2. **The real egress proxy** (`egress_proxy.py`).
3. **A fake provider.** It answers the proxy's readiness probe and logs each model request as a
   `REQ<n> /v1/chat/completions model=<model> stream=<bool>` line.
   - The turn modes use the rig's default provider. Its first answer is a `propose_netlist` tool call
     and its later answers are text.
   - `compact` uses the probe's own provider. Every answer is text, streamed when the request asks
     for a stream, and each line adds `kind=<kind>`:
     - `kind=summary` for a request whose user text holds a `</conversation>` close tag. OpenCode's
       compaction prompt wraps the transcript in `<conversation>` tags. Such a line ends
       `transcript=yes` when that block holds the probe's question and the turn's answer, and
       `transcript=no` otherwise.
     - `kind=title` for OpenCode's title prompt ("You are a title generator", "Generate a title for
       this conversation").
     - `kind=turn` for every other request.

The client is `opencode_client.OpenCodeClient` itself. It runs in a throwaway container from the same
image on the rig network, the way the jail integration tests run it. The jail's config, as committed
(the rig supplies both `{env:…}` values):

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "autoupdate": false,
  "plugin": [],
  "provider": {
    "swxtch-egress": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "name": "swXtch egress proxy",
      "options": {
        "baseURL": "{env:OPENCODE_PROXY_BASE_URL}",
        "apiKey": "{env:OPENCODE_PROXY_CAPABILITY}"
      },
      "models": {
        "accounts/fireworks/models/deepseek-v4p1-flash": {
          "name": "DeepSeek V4.1 Flash"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

It sets no top-level `model` and no `small_model`. A V2 session created without a model relies on
the catalog's default. A compaction summary runs on the session's small model, which falls back to
the primary model when none is set.

## Prerequisites

- **Docker** with BuildKit, and network access to github.com while building. The Dockerfile
  downloads the release asset.
- **`gh`**, authenticated, to read the release's `.sha256` companion and asset digest.
- **Python 3.10 or later**, with `pytest` importable, because the rig module imports it.
- **A swx-abbe checkout.**
  - Measured at swxtchio/swx-abbe#1951's head, `1c6b3582dab3ecef9081dca516102e4c9786f7f4`. Its
    Dockerfile pins `v1.18.32-swxtch.cd3f0ce2`.
  - `main` has the same `_brain_rig(provider_code=...)` signature and the same Dockerfile apart from
    its pin defaults, which the build below overrides.
- **On a snap-Docker host,** `TMPDIR` must be a non-hidden directory under `$HOME`, because snap
  Docker cannot read `/tmp` or hidden directories. The repository checkout must also sit on such a
  path. Elsewhere the default `TMPDIR` is fine.

## 1. Build the jail image for any release tag

The image is built from the checkout's `jail/Dockerfile.jail`. Only the asset name is swapped to the
host's architecture. The Dockerfile stops unless the archive matches `OPENCODE_ARCHIVE_SHA256` and
`opencode --version` prints exactly `OPENCODE_VERSION`. On an amd64 host the `sed` changes nothing.
To test #1953's fix, set `TAG` to the swx-opencode release that carries swxtchio/swx-opencode#354.

```bash
cd <swx-abbe checkout>/components/orch/services/opencode-variant
TAG=v1.18.32-swxtch.cd3f0ce2            # any swxtchio/swx-opencode release tag
VERSION="${TAG#v}"                       # the version the binary must report
case "$(uname -m)" in
  x86_64|amd64)  ASSET=opencode-linux-x64.tar.gz ;;
  aarch64|arm64) ASSET=opencode-linux-arm64.tar.gz ;;
esac
SHA="$(gh release download "$TAG" -R swxtchio/swx-opencode -p "$ASSET.sha256" -O - | cut -d' ' -f1)"
test "$(gh release view "$TAG" -R swxtchio/swx-opencode --json assets \
        --jq ".assets[] | select(.name == \"$ASSET\") | .digest")" = "sha256:$SHA"
sed "s/opencode-linux-x64\.tar\.gz/$ASSET/g" jail/Dockerfile.jail |
  DOCKER_BUILDKIT=1 docker build --progress=plain -f - \
    -t "opencode-variant-jail:v2-egress-$VERSION" \
    --build-arg OPENCODE_RELEASE_TAG="$TAG" \
    --build-arg OPENCODE_ARCHIVE_SHA256="$SHA" \
    --build-arg OPENCODE_VERSION="$VERSION" \
    --build-arg GIT_COMMIT="$(git rev-parse HEAD)" \
    .
```

A first build logs `/tmp/<asset>: OK` in the release-install step. For `cd3f0ce2`,
`VERSION=1.18.32-swxtch.cd3f0ce2`, and the digests are:

| `ASSET` | `SHA` |
| --- | --- |
| `opencode-linux-x64.tar.gz` | `650506db6511c7a3069f1ff4e7cf732b2fdab4c7e056ae2fe7fd258d5eeca414` |
| `opencode-linux-arm64.tar.gz` | `11382c4b6e715e3b2b58628ea96ee53fe0e185361083306313e87ed8913b352f` |

## 2. Save the probe

Save it verbatim. It imports the rig from the checkout, so it may live anywhere.

```bash
cat > ~/jail_v2_egress_probe.py <<'PROBE'
#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Jail-boundary acceptance probe for swxtchio/swx-abbe#1952 (V2 egress) and #1953 (V2 compaction).

Runs the swx-abbe jail integration rig: the real jail daemon started by the image's own entrypoint,
the real egress proxy, and a fake provider. The client is opencode_client.OpenCodeClient itself,
run in a container on the rig's internal network, as the jail integration tests run it.

Usage, from the root of a swx-abbe checkout (or with SWX_ABBE_CHECKOUT set to one):
    python3 jail_v2_egress_probe.py v1-control v2 v2-named compact

Modes:
    v1-control  a V1 turn (OpenCodeClient.open_turn); shows the rig's egress path works
    v2          the V2 calls exactly as opencode_client.py sends them: create_session_v2(), then
                prompt_session_v2(session, "msg_...", {"text": ...})          <- the #1952 case
    v2-named    the same create with the session's model named (not sent by opencode_client.py today)
    compact     a V2 turn as in v2, settled with wait_session_v2, then the V2 compact call,
                POST /api/session/{id}/compact with no body                    <- the #1953 case

v1-control, v2 and v2-named run on the rig's default provider. They pass when it received a
chat-completions request for the egress model.

compact runs on this probe's own provider, which answers every request with text and logs what each
request is: the turn, a title, or a summary request (one whose user text holds OpenCode's
<conversation> block). It passes only when all of these hold:
    - the turn reached the provider and wait_session_v2 reported it completed;
    - the compact call answered 200 or 204;
    - the provider received a summary request carrying this session's turn;
    - the session history records a manual session.next.compaction.ended whose text is the
      provider's summary.
A 503, and a 204 that asked no model, both fail.

Each mode prints RESULT: PASS or RESULT: FAIL. The exit status is 0 only when every requested mode
passed.
"""

import json
import os
import subprocess
import sys
from pathlib import Path

ROOT = Path(os.environ.get("SWX_ABBE_CHECKOUT", ".")).resolve()
VARIANT = ROOT / "components" / "orch" / "services" / "opencode-variant"
sys.path[:0] = [str(VARIANT / "tests"), str(VARIANT)]

import test_opencode_jail_integration as jail  # noqa: E402  the rig

MODEL = "accounts/fireworks/models/deepseek-v4p1-flash"
SIGNAL = f"/v1/chat/completions model={MODEL}"
MODES = ("v1-control", "v2", "v2-named", "compact")

QUESTION = "Please describe an SRT input."
ANSWERS = {
    "turn": "An SRT input listens on one UDP port and admits one caller.",
    "title": "SRT input description",
    "summary": "## Objective\n- Describe an SRT input.\n\n## Progress\n"
               "- Answered: an SRT input listens on one UDP port and admits one caller.",
}

# The compact mode's provider. Every request gets a text answer, streamed when the request asks
# for a stream. Each request is logged as REQ<n> <path> model=<id> stream=<bool> kind=<kind>, where
# kind is "summary" for a request whose user text holds a </conversation> close tag (OpenCode's
# compaction prompt wraps the transcript in <conversation> tags), "title" for OpenCode's title
# prompt, and "turn" otherwise. A summary line adds transcript=yes when that block holds this
# probe's question and the turn's answer.
COMPACT_PROVIDER = r'''
from http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer
import json
import os

IDENTITY = os.environ["PROVIDER_IDENTITY"]
QUESTION, ANSWERS = json.loads(__CONSTANTS__)


def texts(request):
    found = []
    for message in request.get("messages") or []:
        content = message.get("content")
        if isinstance(content, str):
            found.append((message.get("role"), content))
        elif isinstance(content, list):
            found.extend((message.get("role"), str(part.get("text", "")))
                         for part in content if isinstance(part, dict))
    return found


def classify(request):
    found = texts(request)
    users = [text for role, text in found if role == "user"]
    if any("</conversation>" in text for text in users):
        carried = any(QUESTION in text and ANSWERS["turn"] in text for text in users)
        return "summary", " transcript=" + ("yes" if carried else "no")
    if any("You are a title generator" in text or "Generate a title for this conversation" in text
           for _, text in found):
        return "title", ""
    return "turn", ""


class Handler(BaseHTTPRequestHandler):
    requests = 0

    def log_message(self, *_args):
        return

    def _send(self, status, body=b"", content_type="application/json"):
        self.send_response(status)
        self.send_header("Content-Type", content_type)
        self.send_header("Content-Length", str(len(body)))
        self.end_headers()
        self.wfile.write(body)

    def do_POST(self):
        request = json.loads(self.rfile.read(int(self.headers.get("Content-Length", "0"))))
        authorized = (
            self.path == "/v1/chat/completions"
            and self.headers.get("Authorization") == "Bearer fake-vendor-key"
        )
        if "swxtch_readiness_probe" in request:
            if not authorized:
                self._send(401)
                return
            self._send(200, json.dumps({
                "readiness": {"provider": IDENTITY, "nonce": request["swxtch_readiness_probe"]},
                "choices": [],
                "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 1, "completion_tokens": 1},
            }).encode())
            return
        Handler.requests += 1
        kind, detail = classify(request)
        model = request.get("model")
        print("REQ%d %s model=%s stream=%s kind=%s%s" % (
            Handler.requests, self.path, model, request.get("stream"), kind, detail), flush=True)
        if not authorized:
            self._send(401)
            return
        answer = ANSWERS[kind]
        usage = {"prompt_tokens": 10, "completion_tokens": 5}
        if not request.get("stream"):
            self._send(200, json.dumps({
                "id": "chatcmpl-compact-rig", "object": "chat.completion", "created": 1, "model": model,
                "choices": [{"index": 0, "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": answer},
                             "finish_reason": "stop"}],
                "usage": usage,
            }).encode())
            return
        frames = [
            {"choices": [{"index": 0, "delta": {"role": "assistant", "content": answer},
                          "finish_reason": None}], "usage": None},
            {"choices": [{"index": 0, "delta": {}, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": usage},
        ]
        body = "".join(
            "data: " + json.dumps({"id": "chatcmpl-compact-rig", "object": "chat.completion.chunk",
                                   "created": 1, "model": model, **frame}) + "\n\n"
            for frame in frames
        ) + "data: [DONE]\n\n"
        self._send(200, body.encode(), "text/event-stream")


ThreadingHTTPServer(("0.0.0.0", 18081), Handler).serve_forever()
'''.replace("__CONSTANTS__", repr(json.dumps([QUESTION, ANSWERS])))

CLIENT = r'''
import json, sys, time, urllib.parse, uuid
sys.path.insert(0, "/src/components/orch/services/opencode-variant")
import opencode_client as oc

endpoint, password, mode = sys.argv[1], sys.argv[2], sys.argv[3]
client = oc.OpenCodeClient(endpoint=endpoint, password=password, directory="/workspace/project", timeout=30)
out = {"mode": mode}


def history(sid):
    events, after = [], None
    for _ in range(50):
        page = client.get_session_history_v2(sid, after_seq=after, limit=100)
        events += page["data"]
        if not page["hasMore"] or not page["data"]:
            return events
        after = page["data"][-1]["durable"]["seq"]
    return events


try:
    if mode == "v1-control":
        turn = client.open_turn(session_id="v1-control", message="Please describe an SRT input.")
        list(turn.events())
        response = turn.accumulator.build_response()
        out.update(status=response["status"], model=turn.accumulator.model_id)
    elif mode == "compact":
        # POST /api/session  {"location":{"directory":"/workspace/project"}}
        sid = client.create_session_v2()["id"]
        out["session"] = sid
        # POST /api/session/{sid}/prompt  {"id":"msg_...","prompt":{"text":"..."}}
        receipt = client.prompt_session_v2(sid, "msg_" + uuid.uuid4().hex[:16],
                                           {"text": "Please describe an SRT input."})
        out["admitted_seq"] = receipt.admitted_seq
        # POST /api/session/{sid}/wait  (no body)
        try:
            out["turn"] = client.wait_session_v2(receipt, deadline=time.monotonic() + 90).status
        except oc.OpenCodeError as exc:
            out["turn_error"] = str(exc)[:300]
        # POST /api/session/{sid}/compact  (no body), sent as interrupt_session_v2 sends its POST
        deadline = time.monotonic() + 120
        try:
            response = client._request(
                "compactSessionV2", f"/api/session/{urllib.parse.quote(sid, safe='')}/compact",
                method="POST", expected_status=(200, 204), include_directory=False, deadline=deadline,
            )
            out["compact_status"] = oc._response_status(response)
            oc._discard_response(response, deadline=deadline)
        except oc.OpenCodeError as exc:
            out["compact_status"] = exc.status
            out["compact_refused"] = str(exc)[:300]
        # GET /api/session/{sid}/history, every page; once the compact call has succeeded, read
        # until a compaction has ended (the call answers after the summary is recorded, so the
        # first read normally has it; 20 s bounds a missing one)
        until = time.monotonic() + (20 if out.get("compact_status") in (200, 204) else 0)
        while True:
            events = history(sid)
            ended = [e for e in events if e.get("type") == "session.next.compaction.ended"]
            if ended or time.monotonic() >= until:
                break
            time.sleep(1)
        out["history_types"] = [event.get("type") for event in events]
        out["compactions"] = [
            {"type": event.get("type"), "reason": (event.get("data") or {}).get("reason"),
             "text": str((event.get("data") or {}).get("text", ""))[:400]}
            for event in events if str(event.get("type", "")).startswith("session.next.compaction.")
            and not str(event.get("type")).endswith(".delta")
        ]
    else:
        if mode == "v2":
            # POST /api/session  {"location":{"directory":"/workspace/project"}}
            session = client.create_session_v2()
        else:
            deadline = time.monotonic() + 30
            body = {
                "location": {"directory": client.directory},
                "model": {"providerID": "swxtch-egress", "id": "accounts/fireworks/models/deepseek-v4p1-flash"},
            }
            response = client._request("createSessionV2", "/api/session", method="POST", body=body,
                                       include_directory=False, deadline=deadline)
            session = oc._v2_data_object(oc._read_json(response, "createSessionV2", deadline=deadline),
                                         "createSessionV2")
        sid = session["id"]
        out["session"] = sid
        # POST /api/session/{sid}/prompt  {"id":"msg_...","prompt":{"text":"..."}}
        receipt = client.prompt_session_v2(sid, "msg_" + uuid.uuid4().hex[:16],
                                           {"text": "Please describe an SRT input."})
        out["admitted_seq"] = receipt.admitted_seq
        events = []
        for _ in range(45):
            page = client.get_session_history_v2(sid)
            events = page.get("data") if isinstance(page.get("data"), list) else page.get("events", [])
            types = [event.get("type", "") for event in events]
            if any(t.endswith(("step.failed", "step.ended", "step.completed", ".idle")) for t in types):
                break
            time.sleep(1)
        out["history_types"] = [event.get("type") for event in events]
        out["steps"] = [
            {"type": event.get("type"), "model": (event.get("data") or {}).get("model"),
             "error": (event.get("data") or {}).get("error")}
            for event in events if str(event.get("type", "")).startswith("session.next.step")
        ]
        try:
            outcome = client.wait_session_v2(receipt, deadline=time.monotonic() + 20)
            out["wait"] = repr(outcome)[:300]
        except oc.OpenCodeError as exc:
            out["wait_error"] = str(exc)[:300]
except oc.OpenCodeError as exc:
    out["client_error"] = f"{type(exc).__name__}: {exc}"[:400]
print(json.dumps(out), flush=True)
'''


def compact_verdict(result: dict, requests: list[str]) -> list[str]:
    """Every unmet compact-mode condition, in the order the calls ran; empty means PASS."""
    unmet = []
    if not any(" kind=turn" in line for line in requests):
        unmet.append("no turn request reached the provider, so the session has no transcript to compact")
    if result.get("turn") != "completed":
        unmet.append(f"the turn did not complete: {result.get('turn') or result.get('turn_error') or result.get('client_error')}")
    if result.get("compact_status") not in (200, 204):
        unmet.append(f"the compact call answered {result.get('compact_status')}: {result.get('compact_refused')}")
    summaries = [line for line in requests if " kind=summary" in line]
    if not summaries:
        unmet.append("the provider received no summary request")
    elif not any(line.endswith(" transcript=yes") for line in summaries):
        unmet.append("no summary request carried this session's turn")
    ended = [entry for entry in result.get("compactions", [])
             if entry["type"] == "session.next.compaction.ended" and entry["reason"] == "manual"]
    if not ended:
        unmet.append("the history records no completed manual compaction (session.next.compaction.ended)")
    elif not any(entry["text"] == ANSWERS["summary"] for entry in ended):
        unmet.append("the recorded compaction text is not the provider's summary")
    return unmet


def run(mode: str) -> bool:
    network = f"jail-v2-egress-{os.getpid()}-{mode}"
    rig_options = {"provider_code": COMPACT_PROVIDER} if mode == "compact" else {}
    subprocess.run(["docker", "network", "create", "--internal", network], check=True, capture_output=True)
    try:
        with jail._brain_rig(network, **rig_options) as rig:
            client = subprocess.run(
                [
                    "docker", "run", "--rm", "--network", rig["network"],
                    "--read-only", "--cap-drop", "ALL", "--tmpfs", "/tmp:rw,size=16m",
                    "-v", f"{ROOT}:/src:ro", "--entrypoint", "python3", jail.JAIL_IMAGE,
                    "-c", CLIENT, rig["endpoint"], jail.SERVER_PASSWORD, mode,
                ],
                capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=300,
            )
            provider = subprocess.run(["docker", "logs", rig["provider"]], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=15)
            daemon = subprocess.run(["docker", "logs", rig["name"]], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=15)
    finally:
        subprocess.run(["docker", "network", "rm", network], capture_output=True)
    requests = [line for line in (provider.stdout + provider.stderr).splitlines() if line.startswith("REQ")]
    errors = [
        line for line in (daemon.stdout + daemon.stderr).splitlines()
        if any(key in line for key in ("Failed to drain", "ModelNotSelected", "ModelUnavailable", "level=ERROR"))
    ]
    client_line = (client.stdout.strip().splitlines() or ["<no output>"])[-1]
    if mode == "compact":
        try:
            unmet = compact_verdict(json.loads(client_line), requests)
        except (ValueError, KeyError, TypeError) as exc:
            unmet = [f"the client printed no readable result ({type(exc).__name__})"]
        passed = not unmet
    else:
        unmet = []
        passed = any(SIGNAL in line for line in requests)
    print(f"=== {mode}")
    print("client:", client_line)
    if client.returncode != 0:
        print("client stderr:", client.stderr.strip()[-800:])
    print("provider requests:", json.dumps(requests))
    for line in errors[-5:]:
        print("daemon:", line[:400])
    for reason in unmet:
        print("unmet:", reason)
    print("RESULT:", "PASS" if passed else "FAIL")
    return passed


if __name__ == "__main__":
    modes = sys.argv[1:] or ["v1-control", "v2", "v2-named"]
    unknown = [mode for mode in modes if mode not in MODES]
    if unknown:
        sys.exit(f"unknown mode(s): {' '.join(unknown)}")
    results = [run(mode) for mode in modes]
    sys.exit(0 if all(results) else 1)
PROBE
```

## 3. Start the rig and run

Run it from the checkout's root. Each mode starts its own rig, runs its calls, reads the provider's
and the daemon's logs, and tears the rig down. A mode takes under a minute.

```bash
cd <swx-abbe checkout>
mkdir -p "$HOME/jail-v2-egress-tmp"
TMPDIR="$HOME/jail-v2-egress-tmp" PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 \
OPENCODE_VARIANT_JAIL_IMAGE="opencode-variant-jail:v2-egress-$VERSION" \
OPENCODE_SERVER_PASSWORD=local-rig-password \
python3 ~/jail_v2_egress_probe.py v1-control v2 v2-named compact
```

With no mode named, the probe runs `v1-control v2 v2-named`. `OPENCODE_SERVER_PASSWORD` is a
throwaway local value. The rig gives it to the daemon and the client, and it is a credential for
nothing else. The fake provider and the proxy use the rig's own fixture values. No real provider or
key is involved.

## 4. The V2 calls, as `opencode_client.py` sends them

`session_pool.py` calls `create_session_v2()` with no id, then
`prompt_session_v2(<native session id>, <gateway msg_ id>, {"text": <prompt>})`. Neither call adds a
`directory` query. On the wire:

```
POST /api/session
Authorization: Basic base64("opencode:" + OPENCODE_SERVER_PASSWORD)
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{"location":{"directory":"/workspace/project"}}

  -> 200 {"data":{"id":"ses_…", …}}
```

```
POST /api/session/<ses_…>/prompt
(the same headers)

{"id":"msg_<16 hex>","prompt":{"text":"Please describe an SRT input."}}

  -> 200 {"data":{"sessionID":"ses_…","id":"msg_…","admittedSeq":1, …}}
```

`compact` then sends two POSTs with no body, so with no `Content-Type`:

```
POST /api/session/<ses_…>/wait
Authorization: Basic base64("opencode:" + OPENCODE_SERVER_PASSWORD)
Accept: application/json

  -> 200 {"data":{"type":"completed","admittedSeq":1, …}}
```

```
POST /api/session/<ses_…>/compact
(the same headers)

  on cd3f0ce2:  -> 503 ServiceUnavailableError "Session compact is not available yet"
                   (service "session.compact")
  with #354:    -> 204 once the summary is recorded
                -> 204 at once when there is nothing to compact
                -> 500 UnknownError when the summary fails or would not fit the summarizing model
```

`wait` is `opencode_client.py`'s `wait_session_v2`. `opencode_client.py` has no compact method yet,
so the probe sends compact through the client's own `_request`, the way `interrupt_session_v2` sends
its POST: no body, no `directory` query, and the session id path-quoted. The OpenCode SDK's
`v2.session.compact` sends the same request.

After the compact call, the probe reads every page of `GET /api/session/<id>/history`. When the
call succeeded, it keeps reading for up to 20 s, until a `session.next.compaction.ended` event
appears. The call answers only after the summary is recorded, so the first read normally has it.

The modes:
- **`v2`** is exactly the create and prompt calls. It is #1952's acceptance case.
- **`v2-named`** sends the same create with
  `"model":{"providerID":"swxtch-egress","id":"accounts/fireworks/models/deepseek-v4p1-flash"}`
  added. That is the shape B-16.7 (swxtchio/swx-abbe#1792) plans to send; `opencode_client.py` does
  not send it today.
- **`v1-control`** is a V1 turn (`OpenCodeClient.open_turn`). It shows that the rig's egress path and
  the provider work, so a V2 failure is V2's own.
- **`compact`** is create, prompt, wait, compact, then the history read. It is #1953's acceptance case.

The turn modes read the history and call `wait` after the prompt for diagnosis only.

## 5. Success signals

**The turn modes** pass when the fake provider logged a line containing:

```
/v1/chat/completions model=accounts/fireworks/models/deepseek-v4p1-flash
```

That line means the turn's model request crossed the jail's wall and the egress proxy and reached
the provider. **#1952 is fixed at this boundary when `python3 ~/jail_v2_egress_probe.py v1-control v2`
exits 0.** The client line's `history_types`, `steps` and `wait` are printed for diagnosis and are not
part of the signal. With the default provider the V2 `wait` reports `failed`: its first answer is a
`propose_netlist` tool call, which fails in the V2 session (`session.next.tool.failed`).

**`compact`** passes only when all four of these hold:
1. A `kind=turn` request reached the provider, and `wait` reported the turn `completed`. This means
   the session has a transcript to compact.
2. The compact call answered 200 or 204.
3. The provider received a `kind=summary` request ending `transcript=yes`.
4. The history holds a `session.next.compaction.ended` with `reason` `manual` whose `text` is the
   provider's summary.

So a 503 fails, and so does a 204 that asked no model. The probe prints one `unmet:` line for each
condition that fails. **#1953 is fixed at this boundary when
`python3 ~/jail_v2_egress_probe.py v1-control compact` exits 0.**

Every mode prints `RESULT: PASS` or `RESULT: FAIL`. The probe exits 0 only when every requested mode
passed.

