### What `compact` prints when it fails

Each `unmet:` line names one condition from §5:

| Output | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `unmet: the compact call answered 503: … Session compact is not available yet` | The release has no V2 compaction. That is `cd3f0ce2` and earlier. |
| `unmet: the compact call answered 500: …` | #354's `CompactionFailedError`: the summary failed, or it would not fit the summarizing model. The daemon logs `failed to compact session`. |
| `unmet: the provider received no summary request`, with the compact call at 204 | The 204 asked no model: the daemon found nothing to compact. |
| `unmet: no summary request carried this session's turn` | A summary request arrived, but its `<conversation>` block did not hold this session's question and answer. |
| `unmet: the history records no completed manual compaction …` | No `session.next.compaction.ended` with `reason` `manual` was recorded within 20 s of the call. |
| `unmet: the recorded compaction text is not the provider's summary` | A compaction was recorded, but not from the summary the provider sent. |
| `unmet: no turn request reached the provider …` or `unmet: the turn did not complete: …` | The session never had a transcript, so the compaction result proves nothing. |
